      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIM",
          "content": "To know the results in the treatment of acute infectious cholangitis (IAC) and to identify risk factors related to morbidity and mortality."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIAL AND METHODS",
          "content": "We reviewed the records of patients with AIC in a 7 year period. Clinical presentation, diagnostic methods and treatment were analyzed."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "There were 85 cases (61% females and 39% males). Abdominal pain, fever and jaundice were the symptoms most frequently observed. Choledocholithiasis was present in 75% of the cases, malignant obstruction in 12% and other causes in 13%. All patients received antibiotics and 74% underwent any form of biliary drainage. There were complications in 32% of the cases and 14% died. Malignant obstruction was related to high risk of death (OR 11.1)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The IAC is a potentially life-threatening disease and is most ominous in cases of malignant occlusion of biliary tree."
        }
      ]},
